  "notes": "This is a: [l403953] pressing variant of the original\nUS release as indicated by \"T1\" etched in the runout areas.\n\nThe text arrangement used on the labels may be different\nthan on other similar versions of this release.\n\nSpine text: \"NEIL YOUNG / HARVEST / MS 2032 0598–Ⓟ1972–WARNER BROS. RECORDS INC.–PRINTED IN US\". Similar Terre Haute pressing with spine text just \"NEIL YOUNG / HARVEST / MS 2032\": [r=25680796]\n\nRecorded at Quadrafonic Studios, Nashville; Barking Town Hall, London, and Broken Arrow Studio #2, Woodside, CA, Jan.-Sept. 1971, \nexcept B4 recorded live at Royce Hall, UCLA, Westwood, CA, Jan. 30, 1971\n\nIssued with a textured gatefold sleeve, and a\ncustom inner sleeve made of matte finish natural paper. \nIncludes a fold out lyric sheet insert.\n\n℗ 1972 - Warner Bros. Records Inc.\n\nRecorded at:\nQuadrafonic Sound Studios—Nashville, Tenn.\nBroken Arrow Studio #2—California\nBarking Town Hall—London, England\nRoyce Hall—UCLA—California\nB4 Live at Royce Hall—UCLA\n\nReprise Records, a Subsidiary and Licensee of Warner Bros. Inc.\n© 1972 Warner Bros. Records Inc.",
